# tests/registry: the suites tests/run reads. One per line:
#
#   name|runtime tools|tier|images
#
# The make target is `run-` and the name, so it is not written here. The
# runtime tools are the external commands the suite needs beyond the build
# toolchain; `-` means none. The tier is `core` for the set `make test` runs
# and `full` for the rest; `tests/run all` runs both. The images are what
# the suite writes under build/images, as globs separated by commas, and
# the field is left out for a suite whose files are named after it:
# `NAME-test*`, `NAME.*`, `NAME-*` and `NAME/*`, and for a second-card
# twin, `NAME-e1000`, the plain suite's names with `-e1000` before the
# extension. The runner refuses a glob two suites declare, and fails a run
# in which a file was made that no suite of the run owns, or that two own,
# so this column is the inventory of what the suites touch. The core tier is chosen
# by two rules: every subsystem of the kernel is exercised at least once, and
# the tier finishes in under two minutes through the pool, which means no
# member may take longer than that on its own.
#
# Order is the schedule order: the pool starts at the top, and a pool finishes
# when its longest member does, so the long suites are listed first.
